<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wifred II of Cerdanya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 970–1050</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wifred II was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerdanya">Cerdanya</a> from 988 to 1035, a brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliba">Abbot Oliba</a> and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernat-i-count-of-besalu">Bernat Tallaferro</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/besalu">Besalú</a>. He founded the monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sant-marti-del-canigo">Sant Martí del Canigó</a>, consecrated in 1009, and his son Wifred became archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narbonne">Narbonne</a>. In 1035 he retired to Sant Martí as a monk, and he died there around 1050.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wifred-ii-of-cerdanya.jpg" alt="Wifred II of Cerdanya" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liber2Ermengol.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
